{:id :EACL-FORMAL-097
 :status :fixed
 :discovered-by :differential
 :seed-or-trace "eacl-rust/EACL-RS-003/glued-keyword"
 :minimized-fixture "fixture.edn"
 :impact :other
 :affected-versions
 ["v8.0.0 commit a698b3bdf15e61be9bfd1324d7d7c67dc82176be"]
 :affected-backends [:shared]
 :root-cause
 "The Instaparse grammar matched keywords as string literals with no word boundary, so 'relationviewer: user' parsed as the keyword 'relation' followed by the name 'viewer'. EACL accepted schemas SpiceDB v1.56.0 rejects, and stored a relation the author never declared."
 :fix
 "Lex names as SpiceDB does: a word is a maximal run of '_', letters and digits, and it is a keyword only when the whole word is one. A keyword glued to a name is one identifier, so 'relationviewer: user' is a parse error and 'nilviewer' is an undefined reference, as in SpiceDB."
 :closing-evidence
 ["eacl.spicedb.compatibility-corpus-test/glued-keywords-test"
  "eacl.spicedb.compatibility-corpus-test/spicedb-verdicts-test"]
 :notes
 "Found by the eacl-rust port (BUGS.md EACL-RS-003), verified against main a698b3bd and SpiceDB v1.56.0."}
